      "content": "It is incredibly exhausting to feel like a hollow version of yourself while desperately wanting the familiar version you just lost, and your desire to stop \"building\" is actually a sign that you are tired, not broken. Please understand that wanting to stop mandatory effort is not failure; it is a healthy signal that you need rest before you can ever truly find or rebuild who you are. You are not wrong for feeling like you are dragging an empty body, but that heaviness is often just grief acting out as fatigue rather than a permanent state of nothingness.",
